title: A party that has to be forgiven before it can be useful

@porozumienie_search
# prose-audit: Grade A — Gowin's search for a place in the opposition is driven by the relationships his own record actually produced, Lewica influences whether he is welcome without owning the decision, and every destination remains reachable rather than one being scripted.
call: poland_normalize
title: Gowin goes looking for an opposition that will have him
subtitle: PSL, Hołownia and KO all have a use for his votes and a reason not to be photographed with him
face-image: img/poland/events/jaroslaw-gowin-2015.webp
new-page: true
view-if: porozumienie_exit_done = 1 and porozumienie_active = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.porozumienie_search_done = 1;
// How welcome he is. His own record is the drag; the relationships built
// during the postal crisis and the Bielan year are the only thing offsetting it.
Q.porozumienie_acceptance = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(
    22 +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.gowin_channel) || 0) * 0.30 +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_relation) || 24) * 0.25 +
    (Q.gowin_break_attempted ? 6 : 0) +
    (Q.oecd_left_support ? 6 : 0) -
    (Q.gowin_returned_2020 ? 8 : 0) -
    (Q.constitutional_bargain_2020 ? 6 : 0)
)));
Q.news_headline =
    "Gowin begins talking to everybody he spent six years voting against";
!}

= Autumn 2021 — The centre-right that does not exist yet

Jarosław Gowin has **[+ porozumienie_seats +]** deputies, no committee, no
money and an idea. The idea is a moderate, pro-enterprise, Christian-democratic
centre-right built out of PSL, whatever **Szymon Hołownia** is assembling, and
Porozumienie — a bloc that could take the voters who are finished with PiS but
will never vote for Donald Tusk.

It is a sound analysis of the electorate and a difficult one to act on, because
the problem with Jarosław Gowin in the eyes of the opposition is Jarosław Gowin.
He was deputy prime minister in the governments that took the Constitutional
Tribunal, the National Council of the Judiciary and the Supreme Court. He voted
for all of it. The people he now needs spent those years being told by their
own voters that anyone who enabled it is finished, and they have to decide
whether the arithmetic is worth the photograph.

[? if porozumienie_acceptance >= 55: There is more goodwill available to him
than he expected, most of it accumulated in rooms where he was useful rather
than in any public act of forgiveness. Kosiniak-Kamysz takes his calls.?]
[? if porozumienie_acceptance < 55: There is almost nothing available to him. He
is received politely, agreed with in private and left off every platform, which
is the treatment the Polish opposition reserves for people whose votes it wants
and whose company it cannot afford.?]

Our own position matters here more than we would like. Lewica cannot decide
where Gowin ends up, but we can decide how expensive it is for PSL and Hołownia
to be seen with him.

- @gowin_after_attack
- @gowin_after_tolerate
- @gowin_after_conditional

@gowin_after_attack
# prose-audit: Grade B — Refusing any rehabilitation is a defensible line with a real strategic cost: it keeps Gowin out of the centrist bloc and therefore keeps his voters where they are.
title: Attack every attempt to rehabilitate him
subtitle: He stays radioactive; so do his voters, who do not come with him
on-arrival: {!
Q.porozumienie_acceptance = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.porozumienie_acceptance) || 40) - 16
);
Q.gowin_channel = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.gowin_channel) || 0) - 12);
Q.progressive_credibility += 4;
Q.psl_relation -= 3;
Q.p2050_relation = (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 0) - 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left reads out Gowin's voting record every time he appears";
!}

Every time he is introduced as a democrat we read the list: the Tribunal, the
Council, the Supreme Court, the disciplinary chamber, and the years he spent
explaining why each of them was fine. He does not get to launder six years in
one press conference.

It is true and it works. It also keeps a bloc of conservative anti-PiS voters
without anywhere to go, which is not obviously what we wanted.

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign

@gowin_after_tolerate
# prose-audit: Grade B — Tolerating him as a useful conservative is the pragmatic route and it costs credibility with the Left's own base rather than with anyone else.
title: Treat him as a useful conservative and say nothing warmer
