= 2023 — The desperate arithmetic of small parties

**Michał Kołodziejczak** has a movement, a tractor, a national profile and no
parliamentary representation. Porozumienie has parliamentary representation, no
movement and no chance of five per cent. Somebody points out that these are
complementary problems, and for several weeks there are meetings.

The programmes do not fit. AgroUnia is agrarian, protectionist and loudly
hostile to the entrepreneurial-liberal economics that is the only thing
Porozumienie has ever been consistent about. But that is negotiable, and both
sides know it.

[? if agrounia_alliance_holds = 1: What is not negotiable is the PiS question, and this version of Porozumienie can answer it. Under Sroka the party has spent long enough being demonstrably outside the governing camp that Kołodziejczak's people can defend the alliance to their own members, and the joint project is registered. It is not a large thing. It is a route into the next parliament for two organisations that had none.?]
[? if agrounia_alliance_holds = 0: What is not negotiable is the PiS question, and Porozumienie cannot answer it. Asked to say plainly that the governments it served were a mistake, its representatives produce a paragraph about difficult compromises in difficult circumstances. Kołodziejczak's people conclude, correctly, that an alliance with a party that will not say that sentence would cost them more voters than Porozumienie could bring. The talks end without a statement.?]

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign

@porozumienie_list_2023
# prose-audit: Grade A — The 2023 placement of Porozumienie and Kukiz'15 is read from the relationships and alignments the whole chain produced, and a party that ends with no committee and no representation is removed from the simulation with its politicians reassigned rather than left as a permanent shell.
call: poland_normalize
title: Where the survivors file their lists
subtitle: Two years of decisions become one line on a ballot paper
face-image: img/poland/events/election-2023-ballot.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.porozumienie_2023_placed = 1;
const acceptance = Math.max(0, Number(Q.porozumienie_acceptance) || 30);
const porozumienie = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "porozumienie";
});
const kukiz = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "kukiz15";
});
// Porozumienie's committee. The centrist bloc is the natural destination, KO
// takes individuals, and an independent run is only rational if it has built
// something real.
if (!Q.porozumienie_active || !porozumienie || porozumienie.mp_count <= 0) {
    Q.porozumienie_list_committee = "porozumienie";
    Q.porozumienie_route_2023 = "dissolved";
} else if (Q.agrounia_alliance_holds && acceptance >= 64) {
    Q.porozumienie_list_committee = "porozumienie";
    Q.porozumienie_route_2023 = "independent";
} else if (acceptance >= 58 && Number(Q.psl_relation) >= 26) {
    Q.porozumienie_list_committee = "third_way";
    Q.porozumienie_route_2023 = "third_way";
} else if (acceptance >= 44 && Number(Q.ko_relation) >= 44) {
    Q.porozumienie_list_committee = "ko";
    Q.porozumienie_route_2023 = "ko";
} else {
    Q.porozumienie_list_committee = "porozumienie";
    Q.porozumienie_route_2023 = "alone";
}
if (porozumienie) {
    porozumienie.list_committee = Q.porozumienie_list_committee;
    porozumienie.electoral_outside_option =
        Q.porozumienie_route_2023 == "third_way"
            ? "places on the Third Way list"
            : (Q.porozumienie_route_2023 == "ko"
                ? "places on the Civic Coalition list"
                : "its own committee");
}
// Kukiz'15 goes where its own two years put it.
const alignment = String(Q.kukiz_alignment || "unaligned");
if (alignment == "pis_current") {
    Q.kukiz_list_committee = "pis";
    Q.kukiz_route_2023 = "pis";
} else if (Number(Q.psl_relation) >= 34 && Number(Q.kukiz_relation) >= 20) {
    Q.kukiz_list_committee = "psl";
    Q.kukiz_route_2023 = "kp";
} else if (Math.max(0, Number(Q.kukiz_programme_credit) || 0) >= 30) {
    Q.kukiz_list_committee = "kukiz";
    Q.kukiz_route_2023 = "alone";
} else {
    Q.kukiz_list_committee = "kukiz";
    Q.kukiz_route_2023 = "spent";
}
if (kukiz) kukiz.list_committee = Q.kukiz_list_committee;
// Tyszka leaves when Kukiz has attached himself firmly enough to PiS that
// there is nothing anti-establishment left to belong to.
Q.tyszka_defected = (alignment == "pis_current") ? 1 : 0;
const tyszka = (Q.rival_person_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "tyszka";
});
if (tyszka && Q.tyszka_defected) {
    tyszka.party = "konf";
    tyszka.organisation = "konfederacja";
    tyszka.loyalty = "Konfederacja";
    tyszka.status = "Konfederacja MP";
}
Q.news_headline = "The committees are registered and the small parties find out what they are";
!}

= July 2023 — Registration

[? if porozumienie_route_2023 = "third_way": Porozumienie files with the centrist bloc. Its people go onto the Third Way list in places that reflect exactly what they brought, which is a handful of deputies and a claim on a slice of conservative anti-PiS voters. It is the outcome Gowin described in 2021 and it took two years, a change of leader and a great deal of forgetting to reach.?]
[? if porozumienie_route_2023 = "ko": Porozumienie does not survive as an organisation, but its politicians do. KO takes the ones it wants onto its own list, individually, on terms that make clear they are being recruited rather than allied with. It is the most anybody was ever going to offer them and it is not a merger.?]
[? if porozumienie_route_2023 = "independent": Porozumienie files its own committee, with AgroUnia beside it and an actual argument to make. It is a long shot and it is a real one, which is more than the party had any right to expect in August 2021.?]
[? if porozumienie_route_2023 = "alone": Porozumienie files its own committee because nobody would take it. It will not clear five per cent, everybody involved knows it will not clear five per cent, and the filing exists so that the party can say it contested the election rather than dissolved before it.?]
[? if porozumienie_route_2023 = "dissolved": There is no Porozumienie left to file anything. It lost its deputies one at a time to parties that could offer them a seat, and the organisation that Jarosław Gowin used to veto a presidential election in 2020 ends without a committee, a congress or a statement.?]

[? if kukiz_route_2023 = "pis": Paweł Kukiz's candidates appear on the Prawo i Sprawiedliwość list. Kukiz'15 remains a separate registered party with its own name, leader and programme, and it is contesting the election as part of somebody else's committee — which is precisely the arrangement Solidarna Polska has had since 2019 and which Kukiz spent six years describing as the disease.?]
[? if kukiz_route_2023 = "kp": Kukiz'15 returns to the committee it walked out of. PSL takes him back because the arithmetic of a threshold is unsentimental, and the two organisations resume an alliance that neither of them enjoys.?]
[? if kukiz_route_2023 = "alone": Kukiz'15 files its own committee on the strength of an anti-corruption record it can actually point to. It is not obviously enough. It is at least the thing he said he would do.?]
[? if kukiz_route_2023 = "spent": Kukiz'15 files a committee nobody expects to matter. Two years of transactional politics have left it with no list agreement, no bloc and no distinguishing achievement, and the organisation will most likely end with this election.?]

[? if tyszka_defected = 1: **Stanisław Tyszka** does not go with him. A man who joined an anti-establishment movement in 2015 declines to end up on the governing party's list, and moves to Konfederacja, where the anti-establishment argument is at least still being made.?]

- @poland_hub: Return to the campaign

@postal_commission_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — The investigative commission is written from what the 2020 chain actually recorded rather than from the historical timeline, so a game in which the postal election was stopped cleanly, forced through or bargained away produces a different inquiry.
call: poland_normalize
title: The postal election is investigated four years late
subtitle: Gowin testifies about a spring whose events depend on what actually happened in it
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-chamber.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 34
order: 20
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year >= 2024 and postal_event_done = 1 and government_party != "pis" and postal_commission_done = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.postal_commission_done = 1;
Q.judicial_legitimacy = Math.min(
    100,
    (Number(Q.judicial_legitimacy) || 40) + 4
);
Q.news_headline =
    "Jarosław Gowin is called to explain the spring of 2020";
!}

= The commission

A Sejm investigative commission takes evidence on the presidential election that
was scheduled for 10 May 2020. Jarosław Gowin is called, and he is the most
useful witness available for the reason that made him inconvenient at the time:
he was inside the government, he objected, and he wrote things down.

**What the record actually shows:** [+ postal_pressure_record +].

[? if postal_outcome = "forced": The commission is examining an election that happened. The packets, the contracts, the printing and the improvised commissions are all documented, and the question in front of it is how an operation begun without legal authority became a binding presidential result.?]
[? if postal_outcome = "protested": The commission is examining an election that happened and was then voided. Its record joins the packet contracts and improvised commissions to the opposition mobilisation, the corrective law and the court decision that reopened the ballot.?]
[? if postal_outcome = "compromise": The commission is examining an election that did not happen, which turns out to be the harder inquiry. There is no annulment to point at and no court decision — only a joint statement issued at eleven at night by two politicians with no legal power to issue it, and a spending trail that ran until the morning after.?]
[? if postal_outcome = "clean": The commission has comparatively little to find. The postponement was lawful, announced and defensible, and what remains is the money spent on packets before anybody stopped it, which is a smaller scandal and an entirely real one.?]
[? if postal_outcome = "constitutional": The commission has to examine something no Polish inquiry has examined before: an amendment to the constitution used to dispose of an inconvenient election, and the votes — including ours — that made it possible.?]

[? if gowin_break_attempted = 1: Gowin is asked about the opposition's public invitation to leave the coalition, which he declined, and about how the invitation was used against his own deputies afterwards.?]
[? if porozumienie_defection_named = 1: He is also asked about the pressure applied to Porozumienie deputies during the spring, a subject on which the opposition has been publishing a running count since September 2020.?]

- @commission_press_gowin
- @commission_institutions

@commission_press_gowin
# prose-audit: Grade B — Pressing Gowin personally produces the most quotable testimony and the least institutional reform, which is the standard trade in a televised inquiry.
title: Press him on his own signature
subtitle: The best television; the smallest institutional result
on-arrival: {!
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.gowin_channel = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.gowin_channel) || 0) - 10);
Q.news_headline =
    "Gowin is asked, repeatedly, why he signed before he objected";
!}

We ask him about the cabinet minutes rather than about his conscience: which
documents he initialled, on what date, and what he understood the legal basis
to be when he did it. He answers most of it, which is more than the other
witnesses manage.

